  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Friday)\nIssued at 129 AM CDT Sat Oct 10 2026\n\nUpper level ridging will build across the Plains this weekend into \nearly next week, in advance of an upper level trough materializing \nalong the West Coast. The ridge will keep our weather dry, along \nwith well above normal temperatures into the first part of next \nweek. The warmest temperatures are expected Monday through \nWednesday, when forecasted highs climb into the low to mid 90s\nfor much of the area. \n\nSouthwest flow aloft develops across the area by the middle of next \nweek, in advance of the upper trough. Still some uncertainty \nregarding how this system will evolve over time by the middle to \nlatter part of next week, as model differences continue. \nNevertheless, rain chances are expected to increase from Wednesday \nthrough the end of next week, along with cooler temperatures as a \nstronger cold front arrives. Model blends continue to show highs \nonly in the 70s for next Friday and Saturday, with lows dropping \noff into the 50s.",
